.TH ERRMSG_WRITE 3
.SH NAME
errmsg_write \- formatted error message output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <errmsg.h>
.PP
.BI "void errmsg_write(int64 " fd ", const char* " err ", const char* " message ", va_list " list ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B errmsg_write
constructs and writes a formatted error message to the file descriptor
.IR fd .
.PP
The function performs the following sequence:
.IP 1. 3
Calls
.BR errmsg_start (3)
to prefix the message with the program name (if available).
.IP 2. 3
Writes the primary
.I message
string.
.IP 3. 3
Iterates through the variable argument list
.I list
(terminated by a NULL pointer), writing each provided string component to the output buffer.
.IP 4. 3
If
.I err
is non-NULL, appends a colon followed by the error string.
.IP 5. 3
Appends a newline character and calls
.BR errmsg_flush (3)
to finalize the output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR errmsg_puts (3),
.BR errmsg_warn (3),
.BR stdarg (3)